== 8.9 Chapter 8 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Agricultural extension is best described as],
  [the teaching of agriculture in schools],
  [the supply of fertiliser],
  [the marketing of produce],
  [a two-way link between research and the farmer]
)

#mcq(2, [The primary objective of extension is to],
  [raise production through the adoption of improved practice],
  [grade produce],
  [sell inputs],
  [collect taxes]
)

#mcq(3, [The extension agent's most effective method for sceptical farmers is],
  [a circular letter],
  [a poster campaign],
  [a result demonstration],
  [a radio broadcast]
)

#mcq(4, [A method demonstration differs from a result demonstration because a method demonstration],
  [shows a harvested result],
  [teaches a skill by performing it],
  [is held at the office],
  [uses only radio]
)

#mcq(5, [Which extension method reaches the largest number of farmers at once?],
  [Farm visit],
  [Office call],
  [Group meeting],
  [Radio broadcast]
)

#mcq(6, [A farm visit is valuable because],
  [it is the cheapest method],
  [the agent sees the problem where it occurs],
  [it reaches the most farmers],
  [it needs no transport]
)

#mcq(7, [A teaching aid is used in extension to],
  [test the farmer],
  [replace the agent],
  [make the message clear and memorable],
  [increase the cost]
)

#mcq(8, [A flip chart is best suited to],
  [a field of a thousand farmers],
  [a radio audience],
  [a small group indoors],
  [a telephone call]
)

#mcq(9, [The extension agent's feedback role is to],
  [carry the farmer's problem back to the research station],
  [collect the loan],
  [sell the farmer's crop],
  [grade the produce]
)

#mcq(10, [A cooperative society is best defined as],
  [a charity],
  [a government agency],
  [a voluntary association of persons who pool resources for a common benefit],
  [a company owned by shareholders]
)

#mcq(11, [The cooperative principle of one member one vote ensures that],
  [control does not follow the size of the shareholding],
  [the largest farmer controls the society],
  [the government appoints the committee],
  [only the rich can join]
)

#mcq(12, [In a cooperative, the surplus is shared in proportion to],
  [the value of each member's trade with the society],
  [the number of shares held],
  [an equal share to all],
  [the age of the member]
)

#mcq(13, [The main weakness of Nigerian cooperative societies is],
  [too few members],
  [a lack of produce],
  [poor management and book-keeping],
  [too much capital]
)

#mcq(14, [A marketing cooperative helps the farmer by],
  [supplying seed only],
  [grading, bulking and selling the members' produce],
  [lending money only],
  [building roads]
)

#mcq(15, [A credit and thrift society is a cooperative that],
  [takes members' savings and lends to members],
  [sells fertiliser],
  [grades cocoa],
  [rents machinery]
)

#mcq(16, [Marketing boards in Nigeria were established to],
  [train extension agents],
  [build rural roads],
  [buy export crops at a guaranteed price],
  [sell fertiliser]
)

#mcq(17, [The marketing boards ceased to operate in the year],
  [1976],
  [1986],
  [2015],
  [1960]
)

#mcq(18, [The Operation Feed the Nation programme dates from],
  [2015],
  [1976],
  [1960],
  [1980]
)

#mcq(19, [The Green Revolution programme was launched in],
  [1986],
  [1980],
  [2011],
  [1976]
)

#mcq(20, [The Agricultural Development Programme (ADP) is known for],
  [fixing the exchange rate],
  [building airports],
  [a state-level extension service with field agents],
  [marketing export crops]
)

#mcq(21, [DFRRI was concerned mainly with],
  [livestock breeds],
  [marketing boards],
  [crop varieties],
  [rural roads, water and electrification]
)

#mcq(22, [The Anchor Borrowers' Programme links],
  [cooperatives to government],
  [banks to importers],
  [extension agents to schools],
  [smallholder farmers to a processor who supplies inputs and buys the harvest]
)

#mcq(23, [The Anchor Borrowers' Programme dates from],
  [2011],
  [1976],
  [2015],
  [1980]
)

#mcq(24, [NIRSAL was established to],
  [grade produce],
  [train farmers],
  [share the risk of bank lending to agriculture],
  [buy the harvest]
)

#mcq(25, [The Agricultural Transformation Agenda (ATA) is associated with],
  [the marketing board],
  [value chains and the e-wallet input system],
  [the Green Revolution only],
  [rural roads]
)

#mcq(26, [Agricultural insurance is important because it],
  [fixes the price],
  [protects the farmer against a loss too large to bear],
  [guarantees a profit],
  [replaces extension]
)

#mcq(27, [The premium in an insurance policy is],
  [the profit],
  [the amount the farmer pays for cover],
  [the sum insured],
  [the value of the crop]
)

#mcq(28, [The cheapest source of credit for a smallholder is usually],
  [a microfinance bank],
  [a moneylender],
  [a cooperative society],
  [a commercial bank]
)

#mcq(29, [A moneylender is an example of],
  [a subsidy],
  [formal credit],
  [insurance],
  [informal credit]
)

#mcq(30, [Esusu or ajo is],
  [a marketing board],
  [a government loan],
  [an insurance scheme],
  [a rotating savings club]
)

#mcq(31, [The major problem of formal credit for farmers is],
  [the refusal to lend to anyone],
  [the absence of banks],
  [the size of the loans],
  [the demand for collateral and the high interest rate]
)

#mcq(32, [A subsidy on fertiliser is intended to],
  [raise the price of the harvest],
  [lower the cost of an input and raise its use],
  [increase the export],
  [reduce the number of farmers]
)

#mcq(33, [A policy fails most often because],
  [the soil is too fertile],
  [the harvest is too large],
  [the farmers are lazy],
  [the input arrives after the planting season]
)

#mcq(34, [The extension agent's teaching aids include],
  [posters, charts, models and demonstration plots],
  [fertiliser and seed],
  [tractors and ploughs],
  [loans and insurance]
)

#mcq(35, [A farmer group is important to extension because],
  [it pays the tax],
  [the members learn from one another and share the cost],
  [it replaces the agent],
  [it fixes the price]
)

#mcq(36, [The commodity exchange is important because it],
  [builds the roads],
  [fixes the exchange rate],
  [buys all the harvest],
  [creates a standard contract and a visible price]
)

#mcq(37, [The All Farmers Association of Nigeria (AFAN) exists to],
  [represent farmers' interests and lobby government],
  [grade produce],
  [sell fertiliser],
  [train extension agents]
)

#mcq(38, [Strategic grain reserves are held by government to],
  [export the grain],
  [feed the army only],
  [raise the price],
  [stabilise supply and price between seasons]
)

#mcq(39, [The most important characteristic of an extension agent is],
  [a university degree],
  [a motorcycle],
  [the ability to communicate with farmers and win their trust],
  [a government job]
)

#mcq(40, [A cooperative that lends to its officers without records will most likely],
  [earn a large surplus],
  [attract new members],
  [collapse when the funds are not repaid],
  [grow quickly]
)

